  "description": "The founding case of the suite. A -J group holds two primitives, a D key (11 quadlets) and a 0B signature (22 quadlets), so its size is 33, not 2. A second -J group follows it. A parser that counts items reads 33 as 33 primitives and cannot find the second group where it starts. The symbol legends of the Encoding Scheme Symbols Table and the indexed-code symbol table say a count code's digits determine 'the count of the following Primitives or groups of Primitives'; this case rests on the explicit rule at the Count Code tables section instead, and the conflict between the two texts is noted, not resolved, here.",
